1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Section 1

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:02,407
Jim:

3
00:00:02,407 --> 00:00:05,300
Hello, South City Cycling Club.

4
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:06,307
Woman:

5
00:00:06,307 --> 00:00:07,234
Oh, hi.

6
00:00:07,234 --> 00:00:07,284
Er ...

7
00:00:07,284 --> 00:00:11,000
I want to find out about joining the club.

8
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:11,425
Jim:

9
00:00:11,425 --> 00:00:11,850
Right.

10
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:13,975
I can help you there.

11
00:00:13,975 --> 00:00:17,800
I'm the club secretary and my name's Jim Hunter.

12
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:18,275
Woman:

13
00:00:18,275 --> 00:00:19,700
Oh, hi Jim.

14
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:20,178
Jim:

15
00:00:20,178 --> 00:00:24,000
So, are you interested in membership for yourself?

16
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,633
Woman:

17
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:25,900
That's right.

18
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:26,405
Jim:

19
00:00:26,405 --> 00:00:26,910
OK.

20
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:31,452
Well there are basically two types of adult membership.

21
00:00:31,452 --> 00:00:36,500
If you're pretty serious about cycling, there's the Full membership.

22
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,821
That costs 260 dollars and that covers you not just for ordinary cycling

23
00:00:42,821 --> 00:00:49,628
but also for races both here in the city and also in other parts

24
00:00:49,628 --> 00:00:50,600
of Australia.

25
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:50,941
Woman:

26
00:00:50,941 --> 00:00:51,281
Right.

27
00:00:51,281 --> 00:00:54,007
Well, I'm not really up to that standard.

28
00:00:54,007 --> 00:00:58,778
I was more interested in just joining a group to do some cycling in

29
00:00:58,778 --> 00:00:59,800
my free time.

30
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:00,326
Jim:

31
00:01:00,326 --> 00:01:00,852
Sure.

32
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:03,481
That's why most people join.

33
00:01:03,481 --> 00:01:09,265
So, in that case you'd be better with the Recreational membership.

34
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:12,945
That's 108 dollars if you're over 19,

35
00:01:12,945 --> 00:01:16,100
and 95 dollars if you're under.

36
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:16,833
Woman:

37
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:18,300
I'm 25.

38
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:18,690
Jim:

39
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:19,081
OK.

40
00:01:19,081 --> 00:01:20,252
It's paid quarterly,

41
00:01:20,252 --> 00:01:25,719
and you can upgrade it later to the Full membership if you want to,

42
00:01:25,719 --> 00:01:26,500
of course.

43
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,726
Now both types of membership include the club fee of 20 dollars.

44
00:01:31,726 --> 00:01:37,823
They also provide insurance in case you have an accident, though we hope you

45
00:01:37,823 --> 00:01:40,000
won't need that, of course.

46
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:40,384
Woman:

47
00:01:40,384 --> 00:01:40,768
No.

48
00:01:40,768 --> 00:01:44,608
OK, well, I'll go with the Recreational membership, I think.

49
00:01:44,608 --> 00:01:48,448
And that allows me to join in the club activities,

50
00:01:48,448 --> 00:01:49,600
and so on?

51
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:49,981
Jim:

52
00:01:49,981 --> 00:01:50,742
That's right.

53
00:01:50,742 --> 00:01:56,073
And once you're a member of the club, you're also permitted to wear our

54
00:01:56,073 --> 00:01:57,977
kit when you're out cycling.

55
00:01:57,977 --> 00:01:59,500
It's green and white.

56
00:01:59,500 --> 00:01:59,880
Woman:

57
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,160
Yes, I've seen cyclists wearing it.

58
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:05,200
So, can I buy that at the club?

59
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:05,737
Jim:

60
00:02:05,737 --> 00:02:11,109
No, it's made to order by a company in Brisbane.

61
00:02:11,109 --> 00:02:13,794
You can find them online:

62
00:02:13,794 --> 00:02:15,406
they're called Jerriz.

63
00:02:15,406 --> 00:02:16,480
That's J-E-R-R-l-Z.

64
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:24,000
You can use your membership number to put in an order on their website.

65
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:24,340
Woman:

66
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:24,680
OK.

67
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:29,100
Now, can you tell me a bit about the rides I can do?

68
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:29,535
Jim:

69
00:02:29,535 --> 00:02:29,971
Sure.

70
00:02:29,971 --> 00:02:33,888
So we have training rides pretty well every morning,

71
00:02:33,888 --> 00:02:39,982
and they're a really good way of improving your cycling skills as well as

72
00:02:39,982 --> 00:02:42,159
your general level of fitness,

73
00:02:42,159 --> 00:02:43,900
but they're different levels.

74
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:48,559
Level A is pretty fast - you're looking at about 30

75
00:02:48,559 --> 00:02:50,889
or 35 kilometres an hour.

76
00:02:50,889 --> 00:02:57,411
If you can do about 25 kilometres an hour, you'd probably be level B,

77
00:02:57,411 --> 00:03:00,673
and then level C are the novices,

78
00:03:00,673 --> 00:03:04,400
who stay at about 15 kilometres per hour.

79
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:04,806
Woman:

80
00:03:04,806 --> 00:03:05,212
Right.

81
00:03:05,212 --> 00:03:08,053
Well I reckon I'd be level B.

82
00:03:08,053 --> 00:03:08,459
So,

83
00:03:08,459 --> 00:03:11,300
when are the sessions for that level?

84
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:11,724
Jim:

85
00:03:11,724 --> 00:03:14,266
There are a couple each week.

86
00:03:14,266 --> 00:03:16,384
They're both early morning sessions.

87
00:03:16,384 --> 00:03:18,079
There's one on Tuesdays,

88
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:22,316
and for that one you meet at 5.30 am,

89
00:03:22,316 --> 00:03:27,400
and the meeting point's the stadium - do you know where that is?

90
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:27,769
Woman:

91
00:03:27,769 --> 00:03:30,719
Yes, it's quite near my home, in fact.

92
00:03:30,719 --> 00:03:31,088
OK,

93
00:03:31,088 --> 00:03:33,300
and how about the other one?

94
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:33,680
Jim:

95
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,820
That's on Thursdays.

96
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:37,100
It starts at the same time,

97
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:40,900
but they meet at the main gate to the park.

98
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:41,240
Woman:

99
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:44,300
Is that the one just past the shopping mall?

100
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:44,833
Jim:

101
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:45,900
That's it.

102
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:46,300
Woman:

103
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,700
So how long are the rides?

104
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:49,074
Jim:

105
00:03:49,074 --> 00:03:51,695
They're about an hour and a half.

106
00:03:51,695 --> 00:03:56,936
So, if you have a job it's easy to fit in before you go

107
00:03:56,936 --> 00:03:57,685
to work.

108
00:03:57,685 --> 00:04:01,054
And the members often go somewhere for coffee afterwards,

109
00:04:01,054 --> 00:04:03,300
so it's quite a social event.

110
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:03,665
Woman:

111
00:04:03,665 --> 00:04:04,030
OK.

112
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:05,125
That sounds good.

113
00:04:05,125 --> 00:04:10,235
I've only just moved to the city so I don't actually know many people

114
00:04:10,235 --> 00:04:10,600
yet.

115
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:10,956
Jim:

116
00:04:10,956 --> 00:04:13,800
Well, it's a great way to meet people.

117
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,188
Woman:

118
00:04:14,188 --> 00:04:16,900
And does each ride have a leader?

119
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:17,333
Jim:

120
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:17,767
Sometimes,

121
00:04:17,767 --> 00:04:19,067
but not always.

122
00:04:19,067 --> 00:04:21,667
But you don't really need one;

123
00:04:21,667 --> 00:04:26,000
the group members on the ride support one another, anyway.

124
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:26,312
Woman:

125
00:04:26,312 --> 00:04:28,500
How would we know where to go?

126
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:28,871
Jim :

127
00:04:28,871 --> 00:04:34,067
If you check the club website, you'll see that the route for each ride

128
00:04:34,067 --> 00:04:35,180
is clearly marked.

129
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:40,004
So you can just print that out and take it along with you.

130
00:04:40,004 --> 00:04:42,602
It's similar from one week to another,

131
00:04:42,602 --> 00:04:45,200
but it's not always exactly the same.

132
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:45,488
Woman:

133
00:04:45,488 --> 00:04:47,500
And what do I need to bring?

134
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:47,882
Jim:

135
00:04:47,882 --> 00:04:50,173
Well, bring a bottle of water,

136
00:04:50,173 --> 00:04:51,318
and your phone.

137
00:04:51,318 --> 00:04:53,991
You shouldn't use it while you're cycling,

138
00:04:53,991 --> 00:04:55,900
but have it with you.

139
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:56,650
Woman:

140
00:04:56,650 --> 00:04:57,400
Right.

141
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:57,786
Jim:

142
00:04:57,786 --> 00:05:02,036
And in winter, it's well before sunrise when we set out,

143
00:05:02,036 --> 00:05:05,900
so you need to make sure your bike's got lights.

144
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:06,300
Woman:

145
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,100
That's OK.

146
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,300
Well, thanks Jim.

147
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:10,300
I'd definitely like to join.

148
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:13,900
So what's the best way of going about it?

149
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:14,600
Jim:

150
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,000
You can...
